TWO BIASES, pointing in OPPOSITE directions -- a verdict is only
safe if it survives both:
  (a) AGAINST route A: this credits it with PERFECT packing of the
      frame queue, which _run_profile_route_a's submission rule
      (stop once the prefix holds max_trials successes) does not
      give. Real makespan is worse than 1.44*W/cores, so real ra is
      HIGHER than printed.
  (b) FOR route A: this box runs 51 profiles on 32 logical cores,
      1.6x oversubscribed, where the grader runs 51 on 48 (1.06x).
      Under heavy oversubscription short profiles finish early and
      hand their share to the long ones, so D_max/D_mean measured
      HERE is COMPRESSED. The grader's imbalance is >= this, which
      makes real ra LOWER than printed.

